<title>FINLAND: FINNISH SOM ADDS ASKO, TAMRO AND YIT TO FOX INDEX.</title>
<headline>FINNISH SOM ADDS ASKO, TAMRO AND YIT TO FOX INDEX.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish derivatives exchange</p>
<p>SOM Oy said in a statement on Monday it would add the shares of</p>
<p>Asko , Tamro and YIT-Yhtyma to its FOX portfolio and derivatives benchmark idex from August 1.</p>
<p>They would replace Cultor II , Finnair </p>
<p>and TT-Tieto , it said.</p>
<p>The FOX index gauges the 25 most traded shares on the</p>
<p>Helsinki Stock Exchange in the previous six months, and it is</p>
<p>updated twice a year. It is widely used as a benchmark by</p>
<p>investment professionals and investors.</p>
<p>SOM listed the following FOX constituents from August 1:</p>
<p> Merita A    Rauma	   Nokia A </p>
<p> Pohjola B   Rautaruukki  Nokia K </p>
<p> Sampo	 Valmet	  Asko </p>
<p> Finnlines    Enso R	 Kemira </p>
<p> Kesko	  Metsa-Serla B Neste </p>
<p> Tamro	  UPM-Kymmene  Orion </p>
<p> Konecranes   Huhtamaki     Amer </p>
<p> Metra B   Raision Tehtaat </p>
<p> Outokumpu    YIT-Yhtyma </p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
